spans.s:
kúṇapa, n. corpse;
 carcase, carrion;
 🞄a. (ápa) decomposing, stinking like carrion.

KUṆṬ, pp. -ita, blunted, blunt;
 🞄relaxed, jaded;
 ineffectual;
 dull. vi, 🞄pp. blunted.

kuṇṭh-a, a. blunt;
 relaxed;
 dulled: 🞄-tā, f. absence of feeling (in a limb);
 -tva, 🞄n. dulness, obtuseness;
 -a‿aśma-mālā-maya, 🞄a. consisting of a series of blunt stones;
 -ī-kṛ, 🞄blunt;
 -ī-bhū, prove ineffectual.

kuṇḍ-a, n., ī, f. pitcher, jar, pot;
 scuttle;
 🞄round cavity in the graound, round fire-pit;
 m. 🞄bastard of an adulteress;
 -ka, m. n. jar, pot, 🞄pitcher.

kuṇḍa-la, n. ring, esp. earring;
 -lin, 🞄a. wearing earrings;
 coiled;
 m. snake;
 -ī-kṛ, 🞄make into a ring, coil.
